---
// Privacy policy for airothy.com/privacy — the URL App Store Connect points at.
// English only for now; the landing page footer links here from every locale.
const effectiveDate = 'July 25, 2026';
const year = new Date().getFullYear();
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en" dir="ltr">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="How Airothy handles your data: input stays on your local network, no accounts, anonymous usage statistics only."
    />
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#0A1E3D" />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
    <link rel="apple-touch-icon" href="/airothy-icon.png" />
    <link rel="canonical" href="https://airothy.com/privacy/" />
    <title>Privacy Policy — Airothy</title>

    <style>
      :root {
        --bg-deep: #08182f;
        --bg: #0a1e3d;
        --bg-card: #122e57;
        --border: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.09);
        --text: #f5f8ff;
        --text-muted: rgba(245, 248, 255, 0.62);
        --text-faint: rgba(245, 248, 255, 0.42);
        --accent: #8ab9ff;
        --accent-soft: rgba(138, 185, 255, 0.16);
      }

      *,
      *::before,
      *::after {
        box-sizing: border-box;
      }

      html,
      body {
        margin: 0;
        padding: 0;
      }

      body {
        background: radial-gradient(circle at 50% -10%, #1b3a6a 0%, var(--bg) 40%, var(--bg-deep) 100%);
        color: var(--text);
        font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'SF Pro Text', 'Segoe UI', 'Noto Sans',
          'Inter', system-ui, sans-serif;
        font-size: 17px;
        line-height: 1.65;
        -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
        min-height: 100vh;
      }

      a {
        color: var(--accent);
        text-decoration: none;
      }

      a:hover {
        color: #b8d4ff;
      }

      .wrap {
        max-width: 720px;
        margin: 0 auto;
        padding: 0 28px;
      }

      nav {
        padding: 28px 0;
      }

      .brand img {
        height: 28px;
        width: auto;
        filter: brightness(0) invert(1);
        opacity: 0.95;
      }

      main {
        padding: 24px 0 60px;
      }

      h1 {
        font-size: clamp(32px, 5vw, 44px);
        font-weight: 700;
        letter-spacing: -0.02em;
        margin: 0 0 8px;
      }

      .effective {
        color: var(--text-faint);
        font-size: 14px;
        margin: 0 0 36px;
      }

      .summary {
        padding: 24px 26px;
        border-radius: 16px;
        background: var(--bg-card);
        border: 1px solid var(--border);
        margin-bottom: 44px;
      }

      .summary h2 {
        margin: 0 0 12px;
        font-size: 16px;
        font-weight: 700;
        color: var(--accent);
        letter-spacing: 0.02em;
      }

      .summary ul {
        margin: 0;
        padding-inline-start: 20px;
        color: var(--text-muted);
        font-size: 15px;
      }

      .summary li + li {
        margin-top: 8px;
      }

      h2 {
        font-size: 22px;
        font-weight: 700;
        letter-spacing: -0.01em;
        margin: 40px 0 12px;
      }

      p {
        color: var(--text-muted);
        margin: 0 0 16px;
      }

      strong {
        color: var(--text);
        font-weight: 600;
      }

      footer {
        border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
        padding: 32px 0 44px;
        color: var(--text-faint);
        font-size: 14px;
      }
    </style>
  </head>

  <body>
    <nav>
      <div class="wrap">
        <a class="brand" href="/" aria-label="Airothy home">
          <img src="/airothy-wordmark.png" alt="Airothy" />
        </a>
      </div>
    </nav>

    <main>
      <div class="wrap">
        <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p class="effective">Effective {effectiveDate}</p>

        <div class="summary">
          <h2>The short version</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>
              Everything you type and tap travels directly from your iPhone to your Mac over your
              own local network, encrypted. It never touches the internet or any server of ours.
            </li>
            <li>There are no accounts. We don't know who you are.</li>
            <li>
              The iOS app sends anonymous usage statistics through TelemetryDeck. Nothing in them
              identifies you. We don't track you across apps and we never sell data.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <p>
          Airothy is a pair of apps: an iOS app that turns your iPhone or iPad into a trackpad and
          keyboard, and a macOS companion app that receives that input. This policy explains what
          data the apps handle, and how little of it ever leaves your devices.
        </p>

        <h2>Your input stays on your network</h2>
        <p>
          Trackpad gestures, keystrokes, clicks, and scrolls travel straight from your iPhone to
          your Mac over your local Wi-Fi or LAN, on an encrypted and authenticated connection.
          There is no relay server and no cloud component. Airothy works even on a network with no
          internet access at all. <strong>We never see, store, or transmit anything you type or
          tap.</strong>
        </p>

        <h2>Anonymous usage statistics</h2>
        <p>
          The iOS app uses <a href="https://telemetrydeck.com/privacy/">TelemetryDeck</a>, a
          privacy-focused analytics service, to count anonymous events such as app launches,
          feature usage, and whether a trial or purchase happened. Events carry general technical
          context like app version, device model, OS version, and language. TelemetryDeck hashes
          identifiers before storing anything, so this data cannot be tied back to you as a person.
          We use it only to understand which features matter and to improve the app.
        </p>
        <p>
          We do not use advertising identifiers, we do not track you across other companies' apps
          or websites, and we never sell data. This is also why the app never shows Apple's App
          Tracking Transparency prompt: there is no tracking to ask about.
        </p>
        <p>The macOS app sends no analytics at all.</p>

        <h2>Camera</h2>
        <p>
          The iOS app asks for camera access only when you scan the pairing QR code shown on your
          Mac. Scanning happens entirely on your device. No photos or video are captured, stored,
          or sent anywhere.
        </p>

        <h2>Purchases</h2>
        <p>
          Airothy Pro is a one-time purchase handled entirely by Apple through the App Store.
          Apple processes the payment; we never receive your name, payment details, or Apple
          Account. The apps only learn whether Pro is unlocked.
        </p>

        <h2>Data stored on your devices</h2>
        <p>
          To make pairing work, the apps keep a small amount of data locally: the cryptographic
          keys your devices use to recognize each other, the list of Macs you've paired with on
          the iPhone and iPhones you've approved on the Mac, and your settings. This data stays on
          your devices and is never uploaded. Deleting the apps deletes it.
        </p>

        <h2>Children</h2>
        <p>
          Airothy is a general-audience utility and collects no personal information from anyone,
          including children.
        </p>

        <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
        <p>
          If this policy changes, we'll update this page and its effective date. Meaningful
          changes will also be mentioned in the app's release notes.
        </p>

        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Questions about privacy? Email
          <a href="mailto:passlet@icloud.com">passlet@icloud.com</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </main>

    <footer>
      <div class="wrap">© {year} Airothy. Made by easterve.</div>
    </footer>
  </body>
</html>
